                <pb facs="0255" n="135" sameAs="frus:frus1905/pg135"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Chargé Coolidge.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1905-01-17"><hi rendition="#italic">January 17,
                        1905</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Hay informs Mr. Coolidge that Department’s telegram of the 14th instant is
                    not intended to mean that the Government of the United States has adopted the
                    point of view of the Russian Government. In answering the assertion of that
                    government confidence was expressed that neither combatant would violate Chinese
                    neutrality.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
